---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';import sources from '../data/sources.json';import provenance from '../data/provenance.json';import content from '../data/content.json';
---
<Shell title="Sources & methodology" active="sources"><article class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Read the source</span><h1>Sources & methodology</h1><p>{content.methodology}</p><h2>Canonical text</h2><p>Quran text comes from <a href="https://mcp.quran.ai">Quran Foundation's official Quran MCP</a>. Arabic is Uthmani Hafs, <code>ar-uthmani-hafs</code>. English is Marmaduke Pickthall, <code>en-pickthall</code>, whose historical public-domain wording is preserved. New commentary anchors were fetched using <code>fetch_tafsir</code>, edition <code>ar-muyassar</code>, the King Fahd Quran Printing Complex committee's concise Arabic commentary. Commentary summaries are original English paraphrases checked against that retrieved Arabic; full commentary is not republished.</p><p>Hadith references identify the named report on Sunnah.com. Ancient Arabic prayer excerpts are distinguished from Quran text. Their English meanings are our concise renderings from the Arabic, not quotations of modern English hadith translations. Valid narrated variants exist; this is a meaning study, not a complete prayer manual or a ruling on prayer validity.</p><h2>Provenance and reuse</h2><p>Canonical snapshot retrieved {provenance.retrievedAt.slice(0,10)}. Additional commentary and reference checks completed for this batch. Source records, checksums, and edition names ship with each project. Activity groupings and questions are editorial learning aids, not scholarly certification.</p><p class="micro">Snapshot SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">{provenance.snapshotSha256}</code></p><p>Original app code is MIT licensed. DM Sans, Newsreader and Amiri are local SIL Open Font License assets. Other media keep the terms listed below and in their bundled attribution files. No personal blogs are used.</p><h2>References and media</h2><ul class="source-list">{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.label} ↗</a><small>{s.kind} · {s.note}</small></li>)}</ul><button class="button secondary" data-print>Print sources</button></article></Shell>
